INSERT INTO public.story_chapter_i18n (chapter_id, locale, title, body)
SELECT ch.id, 'en',
  $body$How He Talks$body$,
  $body$He never spoke, so he carved instead.

Little wooden tokens, the size of a thumb. A fish meant *the boats go out today*. A cup meant *drink more water*. A sun meant *tomorrow*. A bowl meant *eat something, you look terrible*.

He left them on doorsteps and windowsills. Soon the whole village was reading them.

The children started collecting them. A girl named Marci kept hers in a tin box under her bed.

Marci did not speak either. Not one word, ever, her whole life — which is probably why those two understood each other inside a week. By the middle of summer she had nineteen tokens, and she was the only person in Stillwater Bay who could read every single one.$body$
FROM public.story_chapter ch
JOIN public.story_issue i ON i.id = ch.issue_id
WHERE i.slug = $body$juggernaut-sixty-one-carvings$body$ AND ch.chapter_index = 6;

