INSERT INTO public.story_chapter_i18n (chapter_id, locale, title, body)
SELECT ch.id, 'en',
  $body$The Doctor with the Laugh$body$,
  $body$In July a doctor arrived, though not the kind anyone expected.

He came up the street shouting *Someone call de doctor?* — nobody had — and he was a troll, small and grinning, hung with feathers, beads and little bones, carrying a stick with a skull on it. Zharvakko was a witch doctor, and he said so proudly, twice.

He also laughed. At everything. At bad news, at broken bones, at your temperature. Three patients hid under their blankets the moment they heard him coming.

But Witch Doctor's medicine worked, which nobody could forgive him for.

He needed one thing to make more of it: a grey root that only grew on the far side of the island, past the rocks, where the village had stopped going years ago and did not like to explain why.$body$
FROM public.story_chapter ch
JOIN public.story_issue i ON i.id = ch.issue_id
WHERE i.slug = $body$juggernaut-sixty-one-carvings$body$ AND ch.chapter_index = 7;

